+# Node 3.1 — Likelihood-weighted voting (falsification)
+
+**Verdict: FALSIFIED (prune).** B_dev macro = **0.2820** < 0.294 (node 1.1 threshold).
+
+Mechanism: score each distinct extracted answer by sum of exp(-per-token NLL) over
+its candidates; per-token NLL = ar.<scorer>.nll_sum / ar.<scorer>.n_tokens;
+scorer: dream-base -> qwen7b, diffullama -> llama2-7b (its own AR base), all
+others -> qwen7b. Pick highest-scoring answer; ties -> earliest index;
+all-None / no scores -> 0.
+
+## Dev per-model accuracy (n=200 each)
+
+| model      | lw   | majority | delta   |
+|------------|------|----------|---------|
+| diffugpt-s | 0.0100 | 0.0150 | -0.0050 |
+| diffugpt-m | 0.0050 | 0.0100 | -0.0050 |
+| diffullama | 0.0150 | 0.0000 | +0.0150 |
+| dream-base | 0.6500 | 0.7000 | -0.0500 |
+| llada-base | 0.7300 | 0.7450 | -0.0150 |
+| **macro**  | **0.2820** | 0.2940 | -0.0120 |
+
+## Coordinator prediction check
+
+- dream-base predicted ~0.65 (below plain majority 0.7000): **CONFIRMED — exactly 0.6500**
+- llada-base predicted ~0.71-0.73 (below plain majority 0.7450): **CONFIRMED — 0.7300 (top of band)**
+- Macro below 0.294 -> prune: **CONFIRMED — 0.2820**
+
+Lesson: per-token NLL under the AR scorer carries no usable signal in the
+decisive (split-majority) cases — correct-minority answers have at-or-below-chance
+lower-NLL rates (2/14 dev-dream, 8/18 dev-llada). NLL-weighted voting degrades
+the two models where signal exists (dream, llada) because it downweights the
+plurality's high-likelihood candidates instead of counting them.
